/F2 13 Tf (Appendix B: Rulings and frequently asked questions) Tj T* /F1 11 Tf
T*
(Q: Once a sigil has been claimed, can it be passed to another player or returned to the) Tj T*
(landscape? A: No. A claimed sigil stays with the player who took it until the end of the) Tj T*
(game, even if the cairn beside it is later stranded or blown down.) Tj T*
T*
(Q: What happens to stones on a tile that rain turns into bog? A: They remain on the tile) Tj T*
(but are stranded. Stranded stones score nothing and cannot be built upon.) Tj T*
T*
(Q: Can a ridge line pass through the starting tile? A: Yes. The starting tile has ridge) Tj T*
(edges on all six sides and may join any number of ridge lines.) Tj T*
T*
(Q: Wind is drawn while snow is in effect. Which applies? A: Both. Wind removes stones as) Tj T*
(usual; the frozen ridges stay frozen until the next round ends.) Tj T*
T*
(Q: May a player look through the discard pile? A: Yes, at any time, but the order of the) Tj T*
(discards must not be changed.) Tj T*
